ndow is the opening 12-bar, ~36% bear leg to 1368.42, so the bull-trend label rests only on the last ~34 bars, and the 73 bars before that are balance, not trend.", "The 27 bars ahead of the final push are a two-sided range (2357.18-2680) with heavy overlap and mid-range closes; 2850 is a first-bar probe only 79.00 above 2771, and single-bar breakouts of multi-week range tops often fail and re-enter the range.", "Bar 1787270400000 (445.69 range, close 2515.30, ~255.70 upper tail) followed by a 27-bar stall is spike-high behavior consistent with a temporary exhaustion and a market capped by a range boundary rather than a functioning bull channel.", "The 208.30-point final bar after an extended advance could be a buy climax; a large bull bar that is immediately retraced would mark exhaustion rather than breakout acceptance."], "uncertainty": ["V2 D1 context adapted for the V1 PM input."]}, "management_history": [{"schema": "brooks.management-decision.v2", "role": "POSITION_MANAGER", "decision_time_ms": 1790033400000, "action": "HOLD", "position_ids": ["wf-main-1"], "reason": "State reconciles and no management condition is unmet. One MAIN LONG 0.159 ETH-USDT (wf-main-1) matches its single FILLED entry at 2749.714944 and live quantity, hedge_state is single_main with hedge_size 0, hedge_ratio 0 and unresolved false, open_orders and fills_since_last_event are empty, and margin_health is SAFE (equity 10003.43, available margin 9915.27 USDT). The opted-in long exit experiment applies because applicable_risk_behavior.long_exit_policy is lock_and_wait_nonnegative_net and operation_correlation_id ETH-USDT-1h-1790002799999 equals the snapshot correlation_id with no conflicting risk-behavior field; in 5R mode the host lock is far from triggering (policy_state.projected_exit_net +3.21006 versus allowed_loss_usdt 24.92325, last_lock_proof null). strategy_stop_required is false and stop_limit_is_informational is true, so the empty order list is not an unmet protection condition. 